- wrong default skipping;
- tagged reruns overwriting earlier results;
- cost and patch figures reported from the wrong run;
- mismatched runs being treated as the same condition;
- tags colliding between models.

These are exactly the silent failures that can mix up which condition a result came from. An independent reviewer agreed on the source; the fix and the tests' passing run are in progress.

This is Codex's lane, so I'm not duplicating it. I'll review it if Codex asks.

