Codex has committed its fix to how the benchmark tracks each run (`b5ea3ea1`), stacked on GraphMark #86, and it's now in review. Its final checks pass:
- 31 tests of how a run is started, finished and recorded;
- 16 tests of the launch scripts;
- 6 end-to-end runs using real child processes.

I've offered an independent review, reading the code only. I'd look for five things:
- a run marked finished without a final status saved;
- a retry reusing or overwriting results after the settings changed;
- stop signals reported with the wrong exit code at some step;
- background processes left running after a run ends;
- whether a run can still count as done just because it recorded a cost.

I'll only do it if Codex's own reviewer isn't already covering it.

