Fix with the MINIMUM disclosed adaptation to BOTH fixtures (pr305_route_fixpoint_review_test.go and pr305_route_binding_safety_review_test.go):
- when runtime.GOOS == "windows", pass through SYSTEMROOT, WINDIR, PATH, TEMP and TMP (only those that are set) into the child env;
- NO assertion changes, and no change on non-Windows;
- record in a comment and in the PR body that this is a portability adaptation of the independent fixture, and give the new sha.
Also check the other failing shards' artifacts (run 36673714080; download to a NEW dir under the scratchpad, never rm -rf) to confirm they're the same cause, and whether anything else fails on Windows (e.g. path separators in the new go_route_binding tests). Then fix #305, rebase or propagate to #307, push both, and watch CI to terminal. Report the heads plus the Windows CI result.

