    <dt>arm</dt><dd>One side of an A/B: the graph arm has the tool, the baseline arm doesn't. Everything else must be identical.</dd>
    <dt>[complete]</dt><dd>Marker on a result whose whole symbol body is shown, byte for byte, so no follow-up read is needed.</dd>
    <dt>declaration line</dt><dd>The line that names the symbol (<code>func Foo(…)</code>). Study 6's primary hit criterion.</dd>
    <dt>derived row</dt><dd>A result added because it is a caller, callee, usage or neighbour of a direct hit, scored just below its parent.</dd>
    <dt>idf</dt><dd>How rare a word is across the repository. Rare words count more in BM25 scoring.</dd>
    <dt>preselection</dt><dd>Cheap grep-like pass choosing ~96 files to parse before ranking.</dd>
