Codex review 1212 of 758930d plus the v2.1 work in progress is in: FAIL for freezing as written, not a rejection. Fix everything below, then do the registration wiring, and STOP before launch: no model or claude calls, no runbook block 6/7, and no `claude auth status`.

A. Codex findings (each gets a regression test plus a mutation proof):
1. stage_prior must FREEZE the symbols too. Check the prior task's expected sealed graph binding (its identity's graph inputs sha), copy the symbols into run_dir/memory/inputs, and use only the copy. If you claim identity/receipt are frozen, freeze them as well. Regression: rebuilding suite/graphs/<iid> between task 2 and task 3 must not change task 3's view of task 2; it must fail closed if the hash mismatches.
2. run_pairs: recheck `signalled` after build_memory returns AND at the launch boundary. Regression: a signal during a controlled memory-build callback leads to ZERO launcher calls.
3. The CLI `verify` must run the full check_record envelope validation first (kind, instance_id, block_sha256, lineage_sha256) and bind the ACTUAL verifier/extractor hash, not trust lineage.extractor_sha256. Regression: mutate each outer field and verify fails.
4. Absolute-path exclusion must normalize recognized path operands, including attached option forms (-I/x, -L/x, --foo=/x), and resolve `..` BEFORE containment, so that `<repo>/../../outside` is excluded. Test both of Codex's examples.
5. Read detection must preserve shell newline boundaries (respecting quotes and continuations), so `cd src\ncat a.c` records a read of src/a.c. Add multiline tests.

B. Orchestrator decisions (v2.2; write them into STAGE-M-DRAFT.md with the reasons):
6. Item naming: split each contiguous old-side range at symbol ownership boundaries, so EVERY touched function/method is named. Item = (innermost symbol, sub-range). The 3-item cap and ` (+N more)` stay. The first-line-only naming is withdrawn as lossy (Codex 1212).
7. Section 3 excludes commands that are themselves edits under the M edit rule (lexical + python-write naming a tracked file). They duplicate section 1 and quote patch text.
8. The heading must say the block is prompt input supplied by the memory tool, not "tool output".
9. Pin in §5: eligibility, unknown-usage and zero-denominator rules. A complete-case ratio is never labelled an "all 25" total when any assigned usage is unknown; report the denominators.
10. Name the frozen candidate pool used by regen_cohort (the C/R/L sealed task set), not "every repo".

C. Registration wiring (after A and B are green), modelled on L (943cbf1 / 99a1f14):
- CC_TREATMENT=memory (or equivalent) through pilot-env ENVV and the pilot-inner allowlist, refused unless it has the exact expected value;
- the run_stage M case with --memory-mode;
- GATE_FILES including tools/memory_extract.py and tools/cc_attempt.py;
- seal.STAGES / THRESHOLD ($20) / NAMESPACE pilot8M-s55-eg0d92 / EXECUTION pilot8-M-<date> / EVAL_RUN pilot8M-eval1;
- write_stage_manifest registers the registration view and refuses a bound record;
- cohort_report and rerender support for M (the gold-needle scan must treat memory text as legitimate history);
- runbook blocks for M;
- move the spec text from STAGE-M-DRAFT into CHANGES-fairness.md as §10 and re-pin the spec sha;
- an M continuation-approval file quoting the user's standing statement (same as L's);
- re-seal, the identity dry run over all 50 M cells, sandbox_probe, both suites, mutations.
Give the exact launch command and do not run it.

Rules as before: commit locally, never push, no git stash, no rm -rf with globs, no edits to ART/deps or the C/R/L results/evaluations/runs. Report in the same compressed style: commits, test/mutation counts, seal shas, the identity dry-run result, the launch command, open issues, and the jq-2650 block verbatim after the fixes.

